{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.ParticleInteractions.AtomicityRankOneOrderSeparation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.AtomicityRankOneOrderSeparation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Order.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Group.Nat"],"declarations":25,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.rankOne_tensorGenerationFree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.rankOne_tensorGenerationFree","kind":"instance","line":261,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityRankOneOrderSeparation.lean#L261-L276","doc":"**The bridge premise is satisfiable — the rank-one model realises it.** For a\nsingle fundamental object (`S = PUnit`) with simples indexed by `ℕ`\n(`Sym^k V ↔ k`), the multiplicity map `ι n` is the single count `n`, the\nfundamental object is `simple = 1`, and `ι (simple ⋆) = fundamentalWeight ⋆`.\nThis exhibits a genuine model of `TensorGenerationFree`, confirming the premise\nis **consistent and content-bearing** (not vacuously unsatisfiable, so\n`rankOne_of_chain_of_bridge` is not a vacuous conditional) — while no rank-2\nmodel exists (`no_rankTwo_jetTowerChain`). Providing the *rank-one* instance is\nthe intended model, not a laundered rank-2 fabrication. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.rankOne_of_chain_of_bridge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.rankOne_of_chain_of_bridge","kind":"theorem","line":239,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityRankOneOrderSeparation.lean#L239-L259","doc":"**Atomicity derivation, modulo the bridge premise (PROVED).** Given the\ncategorical→order bridge and the jet-tower **chain axiom** (the\ntensor-generation order on simples is total), the category has **at most one\nfundamental object** — `Subsingleton S`, rank ≤ 1.\n\nThis is the atomicity upgrade's `premise → theorem` step, honestly delimited:\nrank-one follows from exactly **two** named premises — the categorical\ndictionary `TensorGenerationFree` and totality of the tensor-generation order —\nthe latter being the jet-tower ordering axiom the route seeks to establish. No\ninstance of the bridge is fabricated; the implication itself is proved. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.TensorGenerationFree.ι_simple","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.TensorGenerationFree.ι_simple","kind":"theorem","line":237,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityRankOneOrderSeparation.lean#L237-L237","doc":"a fundamental object's multiplicity vector is its own indicator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.TensorGenerationFree.simple","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.TensorGenerationFree.simple","kind":"def","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityRankOneOrderSeparation.lean#L235-L235","doc":"each fundamental object is a simple object. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.TensorGenerationFree.ι_mono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.TensorGenerationFree.ι_mono","kind":"theorem","line":233,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityRankOneOrderSeparation.lean#L233-L233","doc":"the tensor-generation order is preserved by `ι` (a simple dividing another\nhas componentwise-smaller fundamental multiplicities). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.TensorGenerationFree.ι","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.TensorGenerationFree.ι","kind":"def","line":230,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityRankOneOrderSeparation.lean#L230-L230","doc":"multiplicities of a simple object in the fundamental objects. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.TensorGenerationFree.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.TensorGenerationFree.mk","kind":"ctor","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityRankOneOrderSeparation.lean#L228-L228","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.TensorGenerationFree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.TensorGenerationFree","kind":"class","line":216,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityRankOneOrderSeparation.lean#L216-L237","doc":"**Categorical → order bridge (conjectural premise, §3b).** The tensor-\ngeneration preorder on the simple-object index `W` is that of the free\ncommutative monoid on the fundamental-object set `S`: a multiplicity map\n`ι : W → (S → ℕ)` sending each simple to its multiplicities in the\nfundamentals, monotone for the tensor-generation order, under which each\nfundamental object `simple s` has multiplicity vector `fundamentalWeight s`.\n\nThis is a **premise** — no instance is provided; it is the honest remaining\ncategorical content of the atomicity route (`qou-ngwo`). The class carries the\ndictionary's genuine inputs (`ι`, `ι_mono`, `simple`, `ι_simple`); the\ndownstream theorem *derives* rank-one from them, so this is a non-degenerate\n§3b-cond hypothesis class, not a self-assuming projection. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.freeRankTwo_not_isTotal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.freeRankTwo_not_isTotal","kind":"theorem","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityRankOneOrderSeparation.lean#L185-L192","doc":"**Corollary — every free rank ≥ 2 model is excluded.** `Fin 2` (two\nfundamental objects) is not a subsingleton, so the free tensor-generation order\non `Fin 2 → ℕ` is not total. Generalises `rankTwo_generation_not_isTotal` from\n`ℕ²` to the free model on any `Fin r`, `r ≥ 2` (and any non-subsingleton `S`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.freeGen_total_iff_subsingleton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.freeGen_total_iff_subsingleton","kind":"theorem","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityRankOneOrderSeparation.lean#L177-L183","doc":"**Atomicity characterization (free models).** The free tensor-generation order\non `S → ℕ` is total (the jet-tower chain axiom) **iff** there is at most one\nfundamental object (`Subsingleton S`, rank ≤ 1). The sharp order-theoretic form\nof atomicity for free models: *chain ⟺ rank-one*. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.subsingleton_forces_freeGen_total","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.subsingleton_forces_freeGen_total","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityRankOneOrderSeparation.lean#L164-L175","doc":"**Rank ≤ 1 gives the chain axiom.** If there is at most one fundamental object\n(`Subsingleton S`), the free tensor-generation order on `S → ℕ` is total — the\nconverse direction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.freeGen_total_forces_subsingleton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.freeGen_total_forces_subsingleton","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityRankOneOrderSeparation.lean#L151-L162","doc":"**Totality of the free tensor-generation order forces rank ≤ 1.** If the\ncomponentwise order on the free weight monoid `S → ℕ` is total (the jet-tower\nchain axiom), then the generating set `S` is a subsingleton — at most one\nfundamental object. This is the derivation direction for free models:\n*chain axiom ⟹ rank-one*. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.fundamentalWeight_incomparable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.fundamentalWeight_incomparable","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityRankOneOrderSeparation.lean#L142-L149","doc":"**Distinct fundamental weights are incomparable.** For `s ≠ t`, neither\n`fundamentalWeight s ≤ fundamentalWeight t` nor conversely — the obstruction to\na chain whenever there are ≥ 2 fundamental objects. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.fundamentalWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.fundamentalWeight","kind":"def","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityRankOneOrderSeparation.lean#L138-L140","doc":"The weight of the fundamental object indexed by `s`: one copy of generator\n`s`, none of the others. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.piGenLe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.piGenLe","kind":"def","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityRankOneOrderSeparation.lean#L131-L136","doc":"**General free tensor-generation order.** The componentwise (divisibility)\norder on the free commutative weight monoid `S → ℕ` on a generating set `S` of\n`|S|` fundamental objects: `piGenLe f g` says every fundamental multiplicity of\n`f` is ≤ that of `g`, i.e. `f` is a tensor factor of `g`. Generalises `genLe`\n(which is the case `S = Fin 2`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.no_rankTwo_jetTowerChain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.no_rankTwo_jetTowerChain","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityRankOneOrderSeparation.lean#L109-L116","doc":"**Rank-2 independence test — resolution for the free model.** The free rank-2\ntensor-generation model `(ℕ², genLe)` admits **no** `JetTowerChain` instance:\nthe fundamental pair is incomparable, so its generation order is not a chain.\nEquivalently, the chain axiom forces rank-one over the free dominance models —\nthe independence test resolves as **exclusion**, not independence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.instJetTowerChainNatLe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.instJetTowerChainNatLe","kind":"instance","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityRankOneOrderSeparation.lean#L106-L107","doc":"The rank-one tower satisfies the chain axiom. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.JetTowerChain.isChain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.JetTowerChain.isChain","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityRankOneOrderSeparation.lean#L104-L104","doc":"The tensor-generation order on the simples is total — the jet tower is a\nchain. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.JetTowerChain.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.JetTowerChain.mk","kind":"ctor","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityRankOneOrderSeparation.lean#L101-L101","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.JetTowerChain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.JetTowerChain","kind":"class","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityRankOneOrderSeparation.lean#L97-L104","doc":"**Jet-tower chain axiom**, isolated as a class carrying the atomicity content:\nthe tensor-generation order `r` on the simple-object index `W` is a total\norder (a chain). This is the single premise the atomicity upgrade needs the\ncorpus jet-tower ordering axioms to entail. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.atomicity_is_jet_tower_totality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.atomicity_is_jet_tower_totality","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityRankOneOrderSeparation.lean#L88-L95","doc":"**The order-theoretic separation.** The jet-tower chain axiom (totality of the\ntensor-generation order) *holds* for the rank-one tower `ℕ` and *fails* for\nthe free rank-two tower `ℕ²`. Totality is therefore exactly the\norder-theoretic form of the atomicity (rank-one) premise: it admits rank-one\nand excludes the free rank-two model. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.rankTwo_generation_not_isTotal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.rankTwo_generation_not_isTotal","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityRankOneOrderSeparation.lean#L79-L86","doc":"**Rank-two tensor-generation order is not total.** The componentwise order on\n`ℕ²` (divisibility in the free commutative monoid on two generators) fails\ntotality, witnessed by the incomparable fundamental pair — so the free rank-2\njet tower is **not a chain**. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.rankTwo_fundamental_incomparable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.rankTwo_fundamental_incomparable","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityRankOneOrderSeparation.lean#L71-L77","doc":"**The two rank-two fundamental weights are incomparable.** In the free rank-2\ntensor-generation order, the fundamental objects `(1,0)` and `(0,1)` — neither\na tensor factor of the other — satisfy neither `genLe`. This is the\norder-theoretic obstruction to a rank-2 chain. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.rankOne_generation_isTotal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.rankOne_generation_isTotal","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityRankOneOrderSeparation.lean#L64-L69","doc":"**Rank-one tensor-generation order is total.** For a category generated by a\nsingle fundamental object `V`, the simple objects `Sym^k V` are indexed by\n`k ∈ ℕ` and the tensor-generation (divisibility) order is `≤` on `ℕ`, which\nis total: the jet tower is a **chain**. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Atomicity.genLe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Atomicity.genLe","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/AtomicityRankOneOrderSeparation.lean#L58-L62","doc":"The **rank-two tensor-generation order**: the componentwise (product /\ndivisibility) order on the free rank-2 weight monoid `ℕ²`. `genLe a b` says\n`b` is obtained from `a` by tensoring with non-negative powers of *both*\nfundamental objects — i.e. `a` is a tensor factor of `b`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}